      "extract": "SU(5) Minimal non-supersymmmetric version. The minimal SU(5) theory fails for two reasons: • gauge couplings do not unify • neutrinos as massless as in the SM. A simple extension cures both problems: add an extra fermionic 24F [18]. Under SU(3)C ×SU(2)W ×U(1)Y : 24F = (1, 1)0 +(1, 3)0 +(8, 1)0 +(3, 2)−5/6 +(¯3, 2)5/6. The uniﬁcation forces the triplet fermion to lie below TeV, with the color octet around 107 GeV.",
