      "extract": "Left-Right Symmetry L −R symmetric theories [9] are based on the SU(2)L × SU(2)R × U(1)B−L gauge group augmented by parity or charge conjugation. Then: • WL implies WR, • νL implies νR, with mνR of order MR through the breaking of L −R symmetry, • Type-I seesaw: connects neutrino mass to the scale of parity restoration. These facts lead immediately to the new contribution [22] to the neutrino-less double beta decay",
